    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s ally Frederick I proclaimed the kingdom in 1806 and roughly doubled the old duchy's territory.</li><li>The constitution of 1819, agreed with the estates, made Württemberg a leading constitutional state of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</li><li>Within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> it kept its own army corps, posts and railways until the king renounced the throne in 1918.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cannstatter-wasen">Cannstatter Wasen</a>, one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s largest folk festivals, began in 1818 as an agricultural fair founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-i-of-wurttemberg">William I</a> after the famine of 1816–1817.</p></aside>
    </section>

